   "entry": "kernel_maxpool2d_bf16",
   "signature": "void kernel_maxpool2d_bf16(const __nv_bfloat16 *input, __nv_bfloat16 *output, int N, int C, int IH, int IW, int KH, int KW, int SH, int SW, int PH, int PW, int DH, int DW)",
   "file": "slots/maxpool2d_bf16.cu",
   "reference_file": "slots/maxpool2d_bf16.ref.c",
   "semantics": "(bf16) 2D max pooling matching torch.nn.MaxPool2d semantics with padding\nand dilation.\nLayout (NCHW, row-major):\n  input:  [N, C, IH, IW]\n  output: [N, C, OH, OW]  with\n    OH = (IH + 2*PH - DH*(KH-1) - 1) / SH + 1\n    OW = (IW + 2*PW - DW*(KW-1) - 1) / SW + 1\n  output[n, c, oh, ow] = max over kh in [0,KH), kw in [0,KW) of\n    val(n, c, oh*SH - PH + kh*DH, ow*SW - PW + kw*DW)\n  where val(...) returns input[n, c, ih, iw] when 0<=ih<IH and\n  0<=iw<IW, else -INF (out-of-bounds lanes never win the max).\nAll tensors are float32. PH/PW are zero-padding amounts on the\nspatial dims; DH/DW are kernel-element strides (dilation).",
   "seed_source": "hand",
